Sprocket-Rake

Ingredients: ELECTRO SWING + SYNTHWAVE & VAPORWAVE + REBEL, ANGRY & AGGRESSIVE + Banjo
Creative Catalyst: Handmade resonator banjos and synth enclosures built from fallen nickel-iron meteorite fragments and antique harbor clockwork.

Sprocket-Rake is a feral, hyper-kinetic clash of runaway swing shuffles, gated 1980s snare smacks, and detuned, tape-warped vapor pads dragged through caustic analog fuzz. Cutting through the nostalgic haze is the savage, metallic attack of a clawhammer banjo strung with piano wire, spitting rapid-fire syncopated riffs with venomous, blue-collar punk hostility.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 128–138 BPM. A relentless, four-on-the-floor swing groove driven by a sidechained synthwave kick, punctuated by sudden half-time industrial sludge stomps and triplet hi-hat chatter.
- Harmonic Palette: Dark minor blues scales and altered Dorian modes colliding with pitched-down, nostalgic major-seventh synth progressions that buckle under abrasive tape-saturation and dissonance.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Clockwork Gating: Gated snare and percussion hits processed through mechanical spring chambers salvaged from timing mechanisms, clipping heavily into analog console preamps.
  2. Ferrite-Rake Banjo Tracking: An acoustic five-string banjo fitted with high-output magnetic pickups and a meteorite-alloy tone ring, double-tracked through cranked British tube heads and hard sidechained to the kick.
  3. Micro-Chopped Horn Decay: 1930s big-band brass samples slowed down to a woozy crawl, pitch-shifted, and sliced into abrasive, machine-gun staccato bursts.
- Dynamics: Songs open with deceptive, humid vapor-lounge preludes of pitch-wobbly rhodes and distant foghorns before detonating into skull-splitting, high-velocity swung stampedes, held together by sudden tape-stop drops and furious gang shouts.

